\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 Nestl\u233\'00\'E9\uc2  to Cut 16,000 Jobs As a Shift Accelerates\b0\par\par\uc2 By Melissa Eddy \par \uc2 557 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 October 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 6\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The company's new chief executive, \uc2 Philipp Navratil\uc2 , announced the reductions as part of a plan to turn around the world's largest food company.\par \par \uc2 The global food giant \uc2 Nestl\u233\'00\'E9\uc2  said on Thursday that it would shed about 16,000 jobs over the next two years, accelerating a cost-cutting program six weeks after the company fired its chief executive.\par \par \uc2 Philipp Navratil\uc2 , who took over as chief executive last month, announced the changes as part of a wider move to cut 3 billion Swiss francs, or $3.7 billion, in spending by 2027. A previous plan called for 2.5 billion francs in cuts over the same time frame.\par \par \uc2 ''The world is changing, and \uc2 Nestl\u233\'00\'E9\uc2  needs to change faster,'' Mr. Navratil said in a statement. ''This will include making hard but necessary decisions''\par \par \uc2 Nestl\u233\'00\'E9\uc2 , which counts \uc2 Nespresso\uc2 , KitKat, Toll House, Perrier and \uc2 Purina\uc2  among its 2,000 brands, is based in Switzerland and employs some 277,000 people around the globe. It said increased automatization and shared services among divisions would compensate for the lost workers.\par \par \uc2 The cuts will affect workers around the world, with 12,000 of them in white-collar jobs, the company said.\par \par \uc2 Nestl\u233\'00\'E9\uc2  has been seeking to cut costs in the face of stalling growth and a drop in demand from China, which has led to increased pressure from investors.\par \par \uc2 President Trump's sweeping tariffs on imports to the United States, including a tariff of 39 percent on Swiss goods, added further challenges. The United States is \uc2 Nestl\u233\'00\'E9\uc2 's largest market.\par \par \uc2 Shares of \uc2 Nestl\u233\'00\'E9\uc2  rose more than 8 percent in trading in Zurich, as investors welcomed the moves after months of turmoil in the company's leadership.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Navratil vowed to move \uc2 Nestl\u233\'00\'E9\uc2  forward by being ''rigorous in our approach to resource allocation, prioritizing the opportunities and businesses with the highest potential returns.''\par \par \uc2 Analysts welcomed the renewed zeal. It comes as multinational consumer products companies, like \uc2 Nestl\u233\'00\'E9\uc2 , are facing challenges like the jump in prices of raw materials, such as coffee and cocoa beans, as well as a shift in consumer preferences away from processed foods.\par \par \uc2 After several months of largely negative headlines linked to internal scandals and personnel issues at \uc2 Nestl\u233\'00\'E9\uc2 , the company's announcement on Thursday appeared to signal a shift in priorities to focus on sales and innovation, analysts at \uc2 Vontobel\uc2 , an international investment management firm based in Zurich, wrote in a note.\par \par \uc2 They praised Mr. Navratil for ''going in the right direction'' and for his ''strong focus on resource allocation, innovation and a performance mind-set.''\par \par \uc2 Mr. Navratil, a longtime \uc2 Nestl\u233\'00\'E9\uc2  executive, took over for \uc2 Laurent Freixe\uc2 , who was forced out over an undisclosed relationship with a subordinate, which the company said was a breach of its code of conduct. \uc2 Nestl\u233\'00\'E9\uc2 's chairman, \uc2 Paul Bulcke\uc2 , stepped down two weeks later and was replaced by \uc2 Pablo Isla\uc2 , a former chairman of the Spanish apparel company \uc2 Inditex\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the company reported a 4.3 percent increase in sales for the third quarter, driven by higher prices and overall sales volumes.\par \par \uc2 Nestl\u233\'00\'E9\uc2  maintained its growth outlook for 2025, expecting an improvement in sales from the previous year despite the negative effects of tariffs and exchange rates, which include the weakening of the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020251017elah0003p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
