\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Reuters and The Associated Press \par \uc2 459 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 October 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 Job Openings Increase\par \par \uc2 Even as Hiring Declines\par \par \uc2 U.S. job openings increased marginally in August while hiring declined, consistent with lackluster labor market conditions that could allow the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  to cut interest rates again later this month despite resilient consumer spending.\par \par \uc2 Job openings, a measure of labor demand, rose 19,000 to 7.227 million by the last day of August, the Labor Department's Bureau of Labor Statistics said in its Job Openings and Labor Turnover Survey, or JOLTS report. Economists polled by Reuters had forecast 7.185 million unfilled jobs.\par \par \uc2 With the government likely to shut down when funding runs out at midnight on Tuesday, the Labor and Commerce departments said on Monday all data releases, including September's employment report due on Friday, would be suspended.\par \par \uc2 Hiring decreased 114,000 to 5.126 million in August, concentrated in the trade, transportation and utilities industry. Reuters\par \par \uc2 E-COMMERCE\par \par \uc2 Door Dash Adds Delivery By Robot in Some Areas\par \par \uc2 DoorDash\uc2  is expanding its offerings, adding restaurant reservations and robot deliveries in some U.S. markets.\par \par \uc2 The San Francisco-based company, already the largest U.S. delivery provider, announced its expansion plans Tuesday, saying it wants to bring even more business to the merchants it works with and stay ahead of ever-increasing customer demand. \uc2 DoorDash\uc2 's total orders jumped 20 percent to 761 million in the second quarter of this year.\par \par \uc2 DoorDash\uc2 's robots will bring new challenges to the company as it takes on the responsibility for storing and maintaining the devices. But a \uc2 DoorDash\uc2  co-founder, Stanley Tang, said the company needs more delivery options to help fuel its growth.\par \par \uc2 ''The shift to autonomy is happening right now, and \uc2 DoorDash\uc2  is uniquely positioned to do something like this,'' Mr. Tang said Monday. Associated Press\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 Consumer Confidence Plunges in September\par \par \uc2 U.S. consumer confidence declined again in September as Americans' pessimism over inflation and the weakening job market continued to grow.\par \par \uc2 The Conference Board said Tuesday that its consumer confidence index fell by 3.6 points to 94.2 in September, down from August's 97.8. That's a bigger drop than analysts were expecting and the lowest reading since April, when President Trump rolled out his sweeping tariff policy.\par \par \uc2 A measure of Americans' short-term expectations for their income, business conditions and the job market fell to 73.4, remaining well below 80, the marker that can signal a recession ahead. Consumers' assessments of their current economic situation dipped by 7 points to 125.4.\par \par \uc2 Write-in responses showed that references to prices and inflation rose last month, regaining its top position as consumers' main concern about the economy. Associated Press\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020251001ela10002v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
