\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Reuters \par \uc2 482 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 September 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 Fewer New Jobless Claims, But Labor Market Softens\par \par \uc2 The number of Americans filing new applications for unemployment benefits fell last week, reversing the prior week's jump, but the labor market has softened as both the demand for and supply of workers have diminished.\par \par \uc2 Though the report from the Labor Department on Thursday showed fewer people collected unemployment checks in the last week of August, that was likely because many had exhausted their eligibility. The hiring side of the labor market has almost stalled even as layoffs remain relatively low. Demand for workers has slowed, with economists blaming uncertainty stemming from tariffs on imports. At the same time, an immigration crackdown has reduced labor supply, creating what the Fed chair, Jerome Powell, on Wednesday described as a ''curious balance.''\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, economists welcomed the decline in applications as a sign of the economy's resilience. REUTERS\par \par \uc2 AUTOMOTIVE\par \par \uc2 Hyundai to Ramp Up\par \par \uc2 Car Production in U.S.\par \par \uc2 Hyundai Motor\uc2  said on Thursday it aims to produce more than 80 percent of the vehicles it sells in the U.S. in America by 2030, up from about 40 percent now. The change is in response to U.S. tariff policies, as the South Korean automaker ramps up capacity at its Georgia plant.\par \par \uc2 Hyundai, which with affiliate \uc2 Kia\uc2  is the third-largest automaker by sales, said its Georgia factory will reach production capacity of 500,000 vehicles a year by 2028. \uc2 Jose Munoz\uc2 , above right, co-C.E.O. of Hyundai, said that he hopes the U.S. and South Korea can find solutions for short-term business travel for specialized workers, after South Korean workers were detained during a raid at a factory in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Munoz said many of the detained workers had been helping calibrate and test advanced battery production technology at a plant supporting Hyundai's U.S. operations. REUTERS\par \par \uc2 TECHNOLOGY\par \par \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  Plans to Enlarge A.I. Facilities in Wisconsin\par \par \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  on Thursday said it plans to build a second massive artificial intelligence data center in Wisconsin, bringing its spending in the state to more than $7 billion. The new $4 billion project will join a $3.3 billion data center in Mount Pleasant in the southeastern corner of the state, announced last year.\par \par \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  said the initial data center remains on track to open next year and will employ about 500 people at its peak, expanding to about 800 once the second data center is complete.\par \par \uc2 It said with the addition of the second large-scale data center, the site would eventually house the world's most powerful A.I. supercomputer, connecting together hundreds of thousands of powerful chips from \uc2 Nvidia\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  said that it plans to prepay for electrical infrastructure to avoid raising electricity rates, and that it would build solar power elsewhere in Wisconsin to offset its energy use. REUTERS\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020250919el9j00051\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
