\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 PBS\uc2  to Cut 15% of Its Staff After Losing Funding\b0\par\par\uc2 By Benjamin Mullin \par \uc2 273 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 September 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Congress voted this year to strip $500 million in annual funding from public broadcasters, including \uc2 PBS\uc2  stations.\par \par \uc2 PBS\uc2  is cutting 100 positions, or roughly 15 percent of its staff, as a result of the major federal funding cuts to public broadcasting.\par \par \uc2 Paula Kerger\uc2 , the chief executive of \uc2 PBS\uc2 , said in an email to station managers on Thursday that the staff reductions were a last resort. The organization had already frozen hiring, restricted travel and paused pay increases.\par \par \uc2 The cuts include 34 immediate layoffs, the closing of dozens of open positions and reductions made this summer in response to the elimination of federal funding for education programming.\par \par \uc2 ''These decisions, while difficult, position \uc2 PBS\uc2  to weather the current challenges facing public media,'' Ms. Kerger said in her email.\par \par \uc2 Like every public media organization in the United States, \uc2 PBS\uc2  is facing serious financial challenges after Congress' elimination of $500 million in annual federal funding in July. The organization previously said it was cutting its budget by 21 percent and reducing dues for its member stations.\par \par \uc2 NPR is also reducing its budget to provide some stations with relief. Katherine Maher, NPR's chief executive, told Texas Public Radio that the organization was cutting its overall budget by $8 million, a ''first step'' to navigating the crisis.\par \par \uc2 The brunt of the financial crisis is landing on local stations across the United States, many of which rely heavily on federal funding. Dozens of TV and radio stations are in danger of shutting down, and many are applying for grant funding to stay afloat.\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020250906el9600030\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
