\par\par \uc2 STOCKS &AMP; BONDS\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 Wall Street Rises on Investor Hopes for Interest Rate Cuts\b0\par\par\uc2 By The Associated Press \par \uc2 660 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 September 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 U.S. stocks rose to a record on Thursday as Wall Street made its final moves ahead of an update on the job market, one that could clear the way for the cuts to interest rates that investors love.\par \par \uc2 The S&P 500 added 0.8 percent to top the high it set last week. The Dow Jones industrial average rose 350 points, or 0.8 percent, and the Nasdaq composite gained 1 percent.\par \par \uc2 Stocks got some lift from easing pressure from the bond market, where Treasury yields fell after the latest reports on the U.S. job market came in worse than economists expected. One report suggested employers, not including the government, nearly halved their hiring in August from the prior month. Another said that more workers applied for unemployment benefits last week in an indication of rising layoffs.\par \par \uc2 Neither number is flashing a recession, and a third report on activity for businesses in the information and other services industries showed stronger-than-expected growth.\par \par \uc2 The upside for investors of a slowdown in the job market is that it could push the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  to cut its main interest rate for the first time this year at its meeting in a couple weeks. Such cuts can kick-start the economy and job market, though they can also accelerate inflation.\par \par \uc2 So far this year, the Fed has kept its main interest rate on hold because it's been more worried about inflation potentially worsening because of President Trump's tariffs than about the job market.\par \par \uc2 ''The year started with strong job growth, but that momentum has been whipsawed by uncertainty,'' according to \uc2 Nela Richardson\uc2 , chief economist at ADP. She said several things could be behind the slowdown, including ''labor shortages, skittish consumers and A.I. disruptions.''\par \par \uc2 A more comprehensive report on the job market's health during August will arrive on Friday from the \uc2 U.S. Labor Department\uc2 , and it will likely carry much weight with the Fed. Ahead of it, the yield on the 10-year Treasury fell to 4.17 percent from 4.22 percent late Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Last month's grim jobs report, which included massive downward revisions for June and May, sent financial markets spiraling and prompted Mr. Trump to fire the head of the agency that compiles the monthly data.\par \par \uc2 Hewlett Packard Enterprise\uc2  added 1.5 percent after its own better-than-expected profit report.\par \par \uc2 T. Rowe Price\uc2  climbed 5.8 percent after announcing a deal where \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  plans to buy up to $1 billion of its stock, or up to 3.5 percent of all its shares. They're teaming up to offer access to some of the private markets where \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  is an expert to the retirement savers and other investors that \uc2 T. Rowe Price\uc2  serves. \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  added 2.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 On the losing side of Wall Street was \uc2 Salesforce\uc2 , which was the heaviest weight on the S&P 500 despite reporting a better profit than analysts expected. Analysts called the performance solid but suggested some of it may have come from one-time factors. \uc2 Salesforce\uc2 , which helps businesses manage their customers, slumped 4.9 percent.\par \par \uc2 C3.ai\uc2  fell 7.3 percent after reporting a larger loss for the latest quarter than analysts expected. The chairman, \uc2 Thomas Siebel\uc2 , called the results ''completely unacceptable,'' while announcing a new chief executive for the company, Stephen Ehikian. He was most recently acting administrator of the \uc2 U.S. General Services Administration\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Figma\uc2  tumbled 19.9 percent even though the company, which offers a design and product development platform, reported results for the latest quarter that roughly matched analysts' expectations. \uc2 Figma\uc2 's forecasts for upcoming revenue also came close to analysts', but expectations may have been even higher given that its stock came into the day at more than double its $33 I.P.O. price from July.\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020250905el950004i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
